"R17"><label>17. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Mills</surname> <given-names>CE</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Robins</surname> <given-names>JM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lipsitch</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Transmissibility of 1918 pandemic influenza.</article-title><source>Nature</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>432</volume>:<fpage>904</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nature03063</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15602562</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Sertsou</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Wilson</surname> <given-names>N</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Baker</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Nelson</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Roberts</surname> <given-names>MG</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Key transmission parameters of an institutional outbreak during the 1918 influenza pandemic estimated by mathematical modelling.</article-title><source>Theor Biol Med Model</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>3</volume>:<fpage>38</fpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1742-4682-3-38</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17137517</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R19"><label>19. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Keeton</surname> <given-names>RW</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Cushman</surname> <given-names>AB</given-names></string-name> <article-title>The influenza epidemic in Chicago.</article-title><source>JAMA</source> <year>1918</year>;<volume>71</volume>:<fpage>1962</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R20"><label>20. </label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Registrar General</collab> Vital Statistics. In